# Files that must never enter the published archive.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# On 2026-07-13 a single publishing run shipped four packages in this catalog
# with a `build/` directory inside the archive — 15-17 MB each, ~99.9% of it a
# Flutter kernel cache embedding over 4,000 absolute paths from the publishing
# machine. Every stranger who pulled those versions downloaded all of it, and
# published versions are immutable, so they are served forever.
#
# The cause was NOT a missing .gitignore rule. The repo-root .gitignore has
# ignored `**/build/` since 2026-03-04, and `pub publish` honours it when run
# from inside the work tree. Those releases were published from a staging copy
# OUTSIDE the git work tree, where a repo-root .gitignore does not apply. Pub
# then included every file on disk and reported "Package has 0 warnings".
#
# `.pubignore` lives inside the package, so it travels wherever the package is
# copied, staged, or archived. It holds in exactly the condition where the
# repo-root .gitignore silently stops applying.
#
# Do not delete this file to "clean up". It is the countermeasure.

# Build output (the 2026-07-13 defect).
build/

# Tooling / analysis artifacts.
.dart_tool/
coverage/
doc/api/

# Library packages do not ship a lockfile; consumers resolve their own.
pubspec.lock

# Scratch.
*.log

# Repo-only maintenance note for the 0.3.x line. It explains to a MAINTAINER
# why `packages/vehicle_condition_fusion_0_3_x/` exists alongside the 0.5.x
# tree; it is not part of the package a consumer pulls, and it was not in the
# published 0.3.3 archive.
MAINTENANCE.md
